@startuml resource-lifecycle-state
' The retained-resource lifecycle exactly as AbiResourceLifecycle.tla models
' it: a resource is born owning one retain, stays alive while the provider's
' counter is positive, admits callbacks only while alive, and is destroyed —
' permanently — by the release that drops the counter to zero. Copying the
' two words never moves the counter.
' Color: live resource states = VtResource green #DCEDC8 / tint #F1F8E9
'   (#33691E); destroyed = trust-boundary red tint #FFEBEE (#B71C1C);
'   callback activity = intersection orange #FFE0B2 (#EF6C00).
' Source of truth: docs/verification/tla/AbiResourceLifecycle.tla
'   (VT-LIFE-1..6), vinary-tree-interop/docs/abi-reference.md § 5.3,
'   tests/abi_resource_lifecycle_correspondence.rs.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
hide empty description
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
  BackgroundColor #DCEDC8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #F9A825
}

title Resource lifecycle — born owning one retain, destroyed exactly at count zero

state "Live\n<latex>\mathrm{count} > 0</latex>" as Live #DCEDC8 {
  state "Quiescent" as Quiescent #F1F8E9
  state "InCallback\n(one or more holders inside\na vtable operation)" as InCallback #FFE0B2
  Quiescent --> InCallback : enter callback\n<latex>\text{requires an owned retain: } \mathrm{owned}(h) > 0</latex>
  InCallback --> Quiescent : exit callback\n(every path, error included)
}
state "Destroyed\n<latex>\mathrm{count} = 0</latex> — permanent" as Destroyed #FFEBEE

[*] --> Live : provider constructs the resource\n<latex>\mathrm{count} := 1</latex> «the first owner's retain»

Live --> Live : retain\n<latex>\mathrm{count}' = \mathrm{count} + 1</latex>
Live --> Live : release «not the last»\n<latex>\mathrm{count} > 1 \Rightarrow \mathrm{count}' = \mathrm{count} - 1</latex>
Live --> Live : copy the two words\n<latex>\mathrm{count}' = \mathrm{count}</latex> «VT-LIFE-4: not a retain»
Live --> Destroyed : final release\n<latex>\mathrm{count} = 1 \;\land\; \text{no live callback of the releaser}</latex>
Destroyed --> [*]

note right of Live #F1F8E9
  VT-LIFE-1 (LedgerBalanced):
  <latex>\mathrm{count} = \sum_{h} \mathrm{owned}(h)</latex>
  VT-LIFE-2: callbacks imply <latex>\mathrm{count} > 0</latex>
  VT-LIFE-3: <latex>\mathrm{count} \ge 0</latex> always
end note

note right of Destroyed #FFEBEE
  VT-LIFE-6 (NoUseAfterDestroy): destruction
  happens exactly at count zero, excludes
  callbacks, and is never reversed — the two
  words dangle; interface vtable pointers and
  node ids die with the retain that scoped them.
end note
@enduml
